      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it's crucial to consult a healthcare professional before making any decisions, I cannot endorse self-medication with high doses of vitamins or steroids, as these can have serious side effects and may not be appropriate for your specific situation. A sudden onset of facial paralysis should be evaluated by a medical professional whenever possible. Delaying proper medical care could lead to unexpected complications. Seeking prompt professional assistance is the safest course, even if it's an inpatient visit. Avoid self-treatment, as it might aggravate the problem.",
      "source": "target",
